                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                        "entry_id": "82e72110-548c-36aa-8979-9423022e296c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A poem or song having a line or phrase repeated at regular intervals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "deaf9f2e-a7a9-40c0-99a8-ae08a5e1d9af",
                                "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                                "text": "It fell upon a holly eve,\nHey ho, hollidaye!\nWhen holly fathers wont to shrieve,\nNow gynneth this roundelay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f3ef568-1b19-4d52-9c21-c622ac936fae",
                                "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                                "text": "When merry milkmaids click the latch\nAnd rarely smells the new-mown hay,\nAnd the cock hath sung beneath the thatch\nTwice or thrice his roundelay,\nTwice or thrice his roundelay;\nAlone and warming his five wits,\nThe white owl in the belfry sits."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "981c2c72-85d5-4c35-986d-63bf98e918f2",
                                "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                                "text": "\"Ay, fool,\" said Tristram, \"but 'tis eating dry\nTo dance without a catch, a roundelay\nTo dance to.\" Then he twangled on his harp,\nAnd while he twangled little Dagonet stood\nQuiet as any water-sodden log\nStay'd in the wandering warble of a brook;[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f57369c8-13a6-4e32-ab98-ca647045491f",
                                "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                                "text": "For then the little birds do sing their sweetest song, all joining in one joyous medley, whereof one may scarce tell one note from another, so multitudinous is that pretty roundelay;[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e162ef4-b98f-4438-ae56-869594f17020",
                                "sense_id": "2c30e5cc-ff39-3de6-8e30-8e7b86104c0c",
                                "text": "\"Instead of being a rollicking bull-necked quarterstaff player with an eye for a wench and a good but untutored voice for roaring a roundelay, he's nothing but a weasel-faced herring-gutted wowser deliberately stuck in a cell to mislead travellers.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
